    "narrative": "Our objective today is to weaponize speed and favorable platoon matchups against a slate of mediocre starters, led by our top-rated play, **Jose Caballero** (75.83). Facing a lefty in Lopez, **Jose Caballero** leverages a +13% platoon edge and a park factor boost to pace our lineup. Close behind are our premier outfield threats: **Corbin Carroll** (74.71) and **James Wood** (73.32). **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong lineup position (#2) and solid xwOBA indicators, while **James Wood** thrives at the top of the order with a +10% volume advantage. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.64) and **Brice Turang** (70.37) also earn elite grades, with **Brice Turang** seeing his floor elevated significantly by the weak 5.17 xERA of Imai. These five represent the core of our daily production strategy, prioritizing high-contact, high-sprint profiles to maximize our scarcest categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the bench was excluding **Austin Riley** (52.30). While his raw talent is superior to several starters, he faces an uphill climb against a quality arm in Lodolo; the marginal efficiency gap between **Austin Riley** and our lower-order starters like **Cole Young** or **Dalton Rushing** favored the latter due to their more advantageous platoon splits and softer pitching matchups. We must also exercise caution with **Seiya Suzuki** (58.32); his status remains subject to a pending lineup confirmation. If **Seiya Suzuki** drops out of the #6 spot or is rested entirely, we will need to pivot to the high-floor options currently held in reserve. Weather remains clear, but the matchup against Painter poses a risk to **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, as his 4.32 xERA is the toughest hurdle our bottom-tier starters will face today. Maintain discipline with our game caps; we are optimized for efficiency rather than pure volume.",
